// r0z4pb probe (bad): the clause resumes in a nested handled body with a reference into a local of the nested body. The rest keeps the reference in `keep`, a local of `main`. The nested body ends after the rest, so the read of `keep` after the `handle` is a read of a dead local.
effect Ask { fn ask() -> &u64 }
effect Other { fn other() }
fn main() {
    let u: u64 = 7
    let keep = &u
    handle Ask { fn ask() {
            handle Other { fn other() { resume(()) } } in {
                let z: u64 = 5
                resume(&z)
            }
        } } in {
        let r = ask()
        keep = r
    }
    print(keep + 1)
}
